   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "DRONA PARVA",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "page_number",
   "box_1000": [
    899,
    48,
    911,
    61
   ],
   "keep": false,
   "reading_order": null,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "3",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "box_1000": [
    99,
    83,
    422,
    126
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 1,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "विपन्नसस्येव मही वाक् चैवासंस्कृता तथा।",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "text": "आसुरीव यथा सेना निगृहीते नृपे बलौ॥२६॥",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "translation",
   "box_1000": [
    86,
    132,
    489,
    271
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 2,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "On the fall of that foremost of the Bharata",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "race, the army of the Kurus resembled the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "heavenly dome stripped of the stars or the sky",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "deprived of the atmosphere; or the earth with",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "her crops blighted; or a discourse teeming with",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "unrefined expressions; or the army of the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "Asuras when in the days of yore, Bali had been",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "(thoroughly) humiliated.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "box_1000": [
    99,
    276,
    396,
    319
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 3,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "विधवेव वरारोहा शुष्कतोयेव निम्नगा।",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "text": "वृकैरिव वने रुद्धा पृषती हतयूथपा॥२७॥",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "box_1000": [
    99,
    325,
    390,
    369
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 4,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "शरभाहतसिंहेव महती गिरिकन्दरा।",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "text": "भारती भरतश्रेष्ठे पतिते जाह्नवीसुते॥२८॥",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "translation",
   "box_1000": [
    85,
    374,
    489,
    513
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 5,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Or a charming lady deprived of her lord; a",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "stream the waters of which had been dried up;",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "or a doe deprived of her mate, surrounded by",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "wolves in the forest or the wide, extended,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "mountain-cave having its lion slain by the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "fabulous Sarabha. Or the slaughter of Janhavi’s",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "son, O foremost of the Bharata race, the army",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "of the Bharatas.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "box_1000": [
    99,
    518,
    420,
    562
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 6,
   "uncertain": true,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "विश्ववाताहता रुग्णा नौरिवासीन्महार्णवे।",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "text": "बलिभिः पाण्डवैर्वीरैरलक्ष्यैर्भृशार्दिता॥२९॥",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": "Some conjuncts in the second line are indistinct."
  },
  {
   "type": "translation",
   "box_1000": [
    86,
    566,
    488,
    651
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 7,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Resembled a tiny bark thrown up and down",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "on the bosom of the mighty main, driven by the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "gale rushing from all sides. It was then greatly",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "harassed by the powerful Pandavas heroes of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "infallible aims.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "box_1000": [
    99,
    656,
    423,
    700
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 8,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "सा तदाऽऽसीद् भृशं सेना व्याकुलाश्वरथद्विपा।",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "text": "विप्रभूयिष्ठनरा कृपणा ध्वस्तमानसा॥३०॥",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "translation",
   "box_1000": [
    86,
    704,
    488,
    773
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 9,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Then that host, with its elephants, horses",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "and car-warriors, was much distressed and",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "exceedingly jeopardised and rendered helpless",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "and terror-stricken.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "box_1000": [
    99,
    778,
    416,
    823
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 10,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "तस्यां त्रस्ता नृपतयः सैनिकाश्च पृथग्विधाः।",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "text": "पाताल इव मज्जन्तो हीना देवव्रतेन ते॥३१॥",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "translation",
   "box_1000": [
    86,
    826,
    488,
    894
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 11,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Then, in that army, bereft of Devavrata, the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "kings and the (common) soldiers, individually",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "struck with panic, seemed to be sinking into the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "nethermost regions.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "box_1000": [
    100,
    900,
    421,
    942
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 12,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "कर्णं हि कुरवोऽस्मार्षुः स हि देवव्रतोपमः।",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "text": "सर्वशस्त्रभृतां श्रेष्ठं रोचमानमिवातिथिम्॥३२॥",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "box_1000": [
    524,
    83,
    866,
    126
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 13,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "बन्धुमापद्गतस्येव तमेवोपागमन्मनः।",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "text": "चुक्रुशुः कर्ण कर्णेति तत्र भारत पार्थिवाः॥३३॥",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "translation",
   "box_1000": [
    510,
    132,
    915,
    295
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 14,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Thereafter the Kauravas remembered",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "Karna, who was equal to Devavrata himself",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "and who was the foremost of all wielders of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "weapons and resplendent like a guest. Then",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "like the heart of a distressed person looking for",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "a friend, their hearts turned towards him",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "(Karna); and, O Bharata, the kings then broke",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "out into exclamations saying, \"O Karna, O",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "Karna.”",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "box_1000": [
    524,
    301,
    862,
    344
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 15,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "राधेयं हितमस्माकं सूतपुत्रं तनुत्यजम्।",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "text": "स हि नायुध्यत तदा दशाहानि महायशाः॥३४॥",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "box_1000": [
    524,
    351,
    862,
    394
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 16,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "सामात्यबन्धुः कर्णो वै तमानयत मा चिरम्।",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "text": "भीष्मेण हि महाबाहुः सर्वक्षत्रस्य पश्यतः॥३५॥",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "box_1000": [
    524,
    400,
    858,
    443
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 17,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "रथेषु गण्यमानेषु बलविक्रमशालिषु।",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "text": "संख्यातोऽर्धरथः कर्णो द्विगुणः सन् रथर्षभः॥३६॥",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "translation",
   "box_1000": [
    510,
    448,
    914,
    640
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 18,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "That son of Radha, that benefactor of ours,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "that progeny of Suta, he that will sacrifice his",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "life in battle, that one of illustrious renown",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "with his followers and friends, has refrained",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "from fighting these ten days; summon him",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "without delay. That foremost of men, that hero",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "of mighty arms, Karna, had been reckoned by",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "Bhishma as only an Ardharatha, in the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "presence of all the Kshatriyas, during the tale",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "of car-warriors of valour and prowess, in spite",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "of his being equal to two Maharathas.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "box_1000": [
    524,
    645,
    865,
    689
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 19,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "रथातिरथसंख्यायां योऽग्रणीः शूरसम्मतः।",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "text": "सासुरानपि देवेशान् रणे यो योद्धुमुत्सहेत्॥३७॥",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "translation",
   "box_1000": [
    511,
    691,
    914,
    797
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 20,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Indeed in that enumeration of Rathas and",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "Atirathas, Karna was thus reckoned-Karna who",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "is the foremost (of all fighters), who is held in",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "high respect by the heroes and who would dare",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "give battle even to Yama, Kubera, Varuna and",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "Indra.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "box_1000": [
    525,
    800,
    874,
    844
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 21,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "स तु तेनैव कोपेन राजन् गाङ्गेयमुक्तवान्।",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "text": "त्वयि जीवति कौरव्य नाहं योत्स्ये कदाचन॥३८॥",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "verse",
   "box_1000": [
    525,
    850,
    838,
    894
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 22,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": false,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "त्वया तु पाण्डवेयेषु निहतेषु महामृधे।",
     "end": "line"
    },
    {
     "text": "दुर्योधनमनुज्ञाप्य वनं यास्यामि कौरव॥३९॥",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "type": "translation",
   "box_1000": [
    511,
    897,
    915,
    950
   ],
   "keep": true,
   "reading_order": 23,
   "uncertain": false,
   "continues_from_earlier": false,
   "continues_later": true,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Out of wrath (excited by this classification",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "of himself) he had thus addressed, O king, the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "text": "son of Ganga - ‘O Kaurava, I will not fight so",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "note": null
  }
 ],
